  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Access to high-end MRI technology in La Paz, Bolivia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Bolivia, there is no possibility to obtain an MRI scan at the internationally required standard level of 1.5 Tesla. Only a few MRI scanners can be found, using outdated technology up to 0.35 Tesla. Low resolution MRI means low quality, as such less functional for most medical indications. Details are missed, about 75% of the injuries cannot be diagnosed by these low-quality MRI. The investments in high-end MRI scans however are too expensive for most hospitals.This project will provide a solution by starting a diagnostic MRI service centre with two mobile MRI units to be parked next to hospitals or outpatient clinics. The centre will provide online diagnostic reports and pictures to the referral doctors, who can deliver medical advice to their patients. Cost of the service will be paid by insurance companies, private hospitals or the patients themselves. The joint venture will work with a social pricing system to assure access also for the poorest people, as a result prices will range between &#x20ac;1 to &#x20ac;150 per scan. The company will have a maximum capacity of 9,000 MRI scans and diagnostic conclusions per year. The centre will be based in La Paz and the mobile units will rotate within the poorer neighbourhoods of La Paz, El Alto and surrounding villages. The joint venture company is formed between Hospital Arco Iris in La Paz and Qmed B.V. of the Netherlands. Through this MRI diagnostic centre the health sector of Bolivia will be uplifted, enabling better medical diagnostic conclusions.</narrative>
  </description>
